  "worked_solution": "In a speed-time graph, the acceleration is given by the slope of the line.\n\nThe line passes through the points $(0,0)$ and $(4,2),$ so its slope is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{2\\,\\text{m/s}-0\\,\\text{m/s}}{4\\,\\text{s}-0\\,\\text{s}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\,\\text{m/s}}{4\\,\\text{s}} \\\\  & =0.5\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration of the bus is $0.5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$",
